  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\nReview of pull request #419 found that in `backend/packages/data/src/observability/systemHealthReport.ts` (currently around line 118), the `permanent` column is computed as `count(*) FILTER (WHERE attempts >= max_attempts) AS permanent`, with no `locked_at IS NULL` guard — unlike the `pending` (line 116) and `overdue` (line 117) columns, which both filter on `locked_at IS NULL`. As a result, a job currently locked for its final attempt (`locked_at` not null, `attempts = max_attempts`) is counted as permanently failed even though it has not yet actually failed.\n\n## Task\n- In `backend/packages/data/src/observability/systemHealthReport.ts`, add a `locked_at IS NULL` guard to the `permanent` column's `FILTER` clause, matching the guard already used by the `pending` and `overdue` columns.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/packages/data/src/observability/systemHealthReport.ts (the `permanent` column's SQL `FILTER` clause only)\n- backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/systemHealthReport.test.ts (new test coverage for the locked final-attempt job, next to the existing \"counts pending, overdue, and permanently-failed queue jobs separately\" test)\n\n## Scope\n### In scope\n- The `permanent` column's filter condition.\n\n### Out of scope\n- The `pending` and `overdue` columns, or any other column in the same query.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A job with `locked_at` not null and `attempts = max_attempts` is not counted in `permanent`.\n- A job with `locked_at` null and `attempts >= max_attempts` is still counted in `permanent`.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=419 key=d67ff9110e -->\n",
